+## Execution budget and tool discipline
+
+This stage has 60 turns. Reserve the last 15 turns for writing the draft and
+running brief_check. Triage the full slate from the supplied snapshots, then
+investigate at most 3 strongest candidates in depth. A smaller well-supported
+set, including zero qualifying views, is valid; never invent evidence or waive
+any mandatory checks to fill a quota. Record why remaining candidates are not
+advanced. Complete and validate views_draft.json by turn 50 and finish.
+
+Use Read, Glob and Grep for file discovery and inspection. For Python, use only
+the exact ADVISOR_PYTHON executable and the allowed advisor module commands.
+Do not use python -c, jq, awk, shell loops, or compound shell commands. Use the
+allowed journal --list and proposals --list tools instead of parsing their
+files with shell scripts. If a tool is denied, do not retry or substitute an
+unapproved shell command; record the limitation, retain fail-closed behavior,
+and finish with only evidence the permitted tools can verify.
 
